{"page": 76, "text": "(Loss) income before income taxes $ (409) $ 311\n(a) Cost of goods sold excludes amortization and impairments of intangible assets. During the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, ten products represented 53% and 50% of total revenues, respectively. 19.SUBSEQUENT EVENTS Bausch + Lomb Chief Executive Officer Transition On October 12, 2026, Thomas J. Appio was appointed Interim Chief Executive Officer of Bausch + Lomb. Mr. Appio will continue to serve as Chief Executive Officer of Bausch Health while assuming leadership of Bausch + Lomb. In connection with this appointment, Brent Saunders departed as Chief Executive Officer and as a member of the Board of Directors of Bausch + Lomb, effective October 12, 2026. Pursuant to a separation agreement, Mr. Saunders will receive a lump-sum cash payment of approximately $75 million. In addition, all of Mr. Saunders\u2019 outstanding equity and equity-based awards in Bausch + Lomb were forfeited and cancelled. Share Repurchase Program On October 24, 2026, the Company\u2019s Board of Directors authorized a share repurchase program pursuant to which the Company may repurchase up to $50 million of its outstanding common shares. The timing and amount of any repurchases will depend on market conditions and other factors, and the program does not obligate the Company to repurchase any particular amount of common shares and may be suspended or discontinued at any time. Redemption of 8.500% Senior Notes Due 2027 On October 28, 2026, the Company announced that its subsidiary, BHA, will issue an irrevocable notice of redemption dated October 29, 2026 to redeem all of its outstanding 8.500% Senior Notes due 2027, representing approximately $643 million in aggregate principal amount. The redemption is scheduled for November 30, 2026 and will be funded using cash on hand. In connection with the redemption, the indenture governing these notes will be terminated.\n42\n"}
