{"page": 101, "text": "Financial Performance Summary of the Three Months Ended September 30, 2026 Compared to the Three Months Ended September 30, 2025 Revenues for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 were $2,941 million and $2,681 million, respectively, an increase of $260 million, or 10%. The increase reflects broad-based growth across all reportable segments and was primarily driven by: (i) improved net realized pricing and (ii) incremental sales attributable to acquisitions, partially offset by lower volumes. These changes in net realized pricing and volumes were partially the result of our decision to exit certain channels, as discussed below. Operating income for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $983 million and $619 million, respectively, and included non-cash charges for Depreciation and amortization of intangible assets of $284 million and $306 million, acquired in-process research and development (\u201cIPR&D\u201d) costs of $0 and $81 million and Share-based compensation of $52 million and $43 million, respectively. The increase in our operating income of $364 million reflects, among other factors: \u2022an increase in contribution (Product sales revenue less Cost of goods sold, excluding amortization and impairments of intangible assets) of $269 million, primarily due to the increase in revenues, as previously discussed; \u2022an increase in selling, general and administrative (\u201cSG&A\u201d) expenses of $39 million, primarily attributable to higher compensation costs and selling expenses, partially offset by lower general and administrative expenses; and \u2022a decrease in Other expense, net of $70 million, primarily attributable to lower acquired IPR&D costs related to the 2025 acquisition of DURECT. Income before income taxes for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $597 million and $218 million, respectively, a favorable change of $379 million. The change is primarily attributable to the increase in our operating income of $364 million, as previously discussed, and a decrease in Interest expenses of $14 million. Net income attributable to Bausch Health for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $436 million and $179 million, respectively, a favorable change of $257 million, which is primarily attributable to a favorable change in Income before income taxes of $379 million, as previously discussed, offset by an unfavorable change in Provision for income taxes of $114 million. Summary of the Nine Months Ended September 30, 2026 Compared to the Nine Months Ended September 30, 2025 Revenues for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 were $8,317 million and $7,470 million, respectively, an increase of $847 million, or 11%. The increase is attributable to growth in our Salix, Bausch + Lomb, Solta Medical and International segments driven by: (i) improved net realized pricing, (ii) incremental sales attributable to acquisitions and (iii) the favorable impact of foreign currencies, partially offset by lower\n"}
