{"page": 114, "text": "Salix Segment: Salix Segment Revenue The Salix segment includes our Xifaxan\u00ae product line which currently accounts for approximately 85% of the Salix segment revenues. Salix segment revenue for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $831 million and $716 million, respectively, an increase of $115 million, or 16%, primarily attributable to: (i) an increase in net realized pricing of $152 million and (ii) the impact from the discontinuation of certain non-promoted products of $13 million, partially offset by a decrease in volumes of $50 million. The revenue increases were partially due to channel mix and other net pricing factors, as well as the timing of channel inventory in the quarter, and were partially offset by lower volumes associated with our decision to exit certain channels, as previously discussed. Salix Segment Profit The Salix segment profit for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $716 million and $570 million, respectively, an increase of $146 million, or 26%. The increase was primarily driven by: (i) higher contribution attributable to the increase in revenues, as previously discussed, and (ii) lower SG&A and R&D expenses. International Segment: International Segment Revenue The International segment has a diversified product line with no single product group representing 10% or more of its product sales. The International segment revenue was $299 million and $286 million for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively, an increase of $13 million, or 5%. The increase was primarily attributable to: (i) an increase in net realized pricing of $10 million and (ii) the favorable impact of foreign currencies of $4 million. International Segment Profit The International segment profit for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $99 million and $90 million, respectively, an increase of $9 million, or 10% and was primarily driven by higher contribution attributable to the increase in revenues, as previously discussed, partially offset by higher SG&A expenses. Solta Medical Segment: Solta Medical Segment Revenue The Solta Medical segment includes the Thermage\u00ae product line, which accounted for over 85% of the Solta Medical segment revenues. The Solta Medical segment revenue for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $165 million and $140 million, respectively, an increase of $25 million, or 18%. The increase was primarily attributable to: (i) incremental sales attributable to the acquisition of Shibo Zhenmei of $29 million and (ii) the favorable impact of foreign currencies of $2 million, partially offset by: (i) a decrease in net realized pricing of $4 million and (ii) a decrease in volumes of $2 million. Solta Medical Segment Profit The Solta Medical segment profit for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was $76 million and $70 million, respectively, an increase of $6 million, or 9%. The increase was primarily driven by higher contribution\n"}
